projects.description:
This introductory meeting is following the letter to the Secretary General Health Malaysia as well as the Director General of Veterinary Services about the Regional Tripartite AMR project funded by the EU for agreement in principle to participate. The agreement to participate was received on 27th January 2023. As part of the project some funding was to go directly through the Tripartite members (WHO in the case of Malaysia) to support some activities related to One Health AMR National Action Planning. A work plan was developed for which this support would be used with the title “Publication and launch of, and multisectoral advocacy for, Malaysia’s second MyAP-AMR 2”. As well as direct in-country support for AMR NAP work, there are several regional activities related to AMR surveillance, private sector engagement and research and innovation. The Regional Tripartite team would be very keen to come to Malaysia as Tripartite (FAO, WHO and WOAH) to meet with appropriate representatives from Ministries of Agriculture and Environment to:  

1. Explain the project;  

2. Agree on work plan activities and timetable for 2023 and 2024;  

3. Review regional activities in 2023 and Malaysia’s interest to participate in or contribute to them;  

4. Identify any synergies between the EU project and other ongoing AMR work in-country.
